Job Description 1

Responsibilities:

- Own post-silicon validation and hardware bring-up for FPGA-based SoC architectures.
- Synthesize, implement, place-and-route, and achieve timing closure using Microchip Libero SoC and Xilinx Vivado.
- Develop processor-based test environments using ARM Cortex-M and RISC-V platforms.
- Develop Embedded C/C++ test cases to validate FPGA hardware IPs.
- Utilize embedded logic analyzers and lab equipment to debug system-level, protocol, and timing failures.
- Perform board bring-up, signal integrity checks, and validation of high-speed serial interfaces.
- Collaborate with RTL design, verification, firmware, software, and board design teams.

Minimum Qualifications:

- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics & Communication, or Computer Engineering.
- Expert proficiency in SystemVerilog, Verilog, and VHDL.
- Strong Embedded C/C++ programming skills.
- Experience with ARM Cortex-M and RISC-V processor-based validation.
- Experience validating AXI4, AHB, APB, PCIe Gen3/Gen4, DDR4/DDR5, SPI, QSPI, and UART interfaces.
- Hands-on experience with Microchip Libero SoC, Xilinx Vivado, Intel Quartus Prime, ModelSim, QuestaSim, and Synopsys Identify.
- Experience using oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, protocol analyzers, and JTAG debuggers.
- Experience with Python and Tcl scripting for automation.

Preferred Qualifications:

- Experience with Secure Boot validation.
- Knowledge of Physical Unclonable Functions (PUF).
- Experience validating Hardware Security IP.
- Knowledge of Static Timing Analysis (STA).
- Experience with thermal and power profiling.
- Experience performing FPGA timing closure.

